+++ b/dev/log/issues/63/pulls/64/github/related-issue-59.json
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+{"body":"## Problem\n\n`docker build .` fails on `main` (`fa90d37`, v0.28.0). Since \"runs as a single Docker container\" is the project's headline deployment story, the release cannot currently be deployed that way.\n\n```\n#13 0.606 error: #[derive(RustEmbed)] folder '/app/ui/dist' does not exist. cwd: '/app'\n#13 0.606   --> src/admin_ui.rs:17:1\n#13 0.606 17 | / /// The built admin UI bundle, embedded at compile time.\n#13 0.606 18 | | #[derive(RustEmbed)]\n#13 0.606 19 | | #[folder = \"ui/dist\"]\n#13 0.606 20 | | struct Assets;\n\n#13 1.037 error[E0599]: no associated function or constant named `get` found for struct `Assets`\n#13 1.037   --> src/admin_ui.rs:43:24\n\n#13 1.684 error: could not compile `link-assistant-router` (lib) due to 2 previous errors\nERROR: failed to solve: process \"/bin/sh -c touch src/lib.rs src/main.rs && cargo build --release\"\n       did not complete successfully: exit code: 101\n```\n\nThe second error is a knock-on: `RustEmbed` cannot expand without the folder, so `Assets::get` never exists.\n\n## Cause\n\n`ui/dist` is deliberately committed — `.gitignore` says so explicitly:\n\n```\n# Admin UI toolchain: `ui/dist` IS committed (it is embedded in the binary),\n```\n\nand it is present in a fresh clone:\n\n```\n$ git ls-files ui/dist\nui/dist/assets/app.js\nui/dist/index.html\n```\n\nBut the Dockerfile never copies it into the build context. The builder stage copies only:\n\n```dockerfile\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY Cargo.toml Cargo.lock ./\nCOPY src/ src/\n```\n\nSo `/app/ui/dist` does not exist inside the image, while it does exist on a developer's checkout — which is why `cargo build` locally succeeds and the Docker build does not.\n\n## Fix\n\nOne line, before `COPY src/ src/`:\n\n```dockerfile\nCOPY ui/dist/ ui/dist/\nCOPY src/ src/\n```\n\nVerified: with that line added and nothing else changed, the image builds and runs.\n\n```\n$ docker build -t router-fixtest .\n...\nnaming to docker.io/library/router-fixtest:latest done\n$ docker images router-fixtest\nrouter-fixtest:latest   164MB\n```\n\nThe resulting container behaves as intended — admin endpoints closed by default:\n\n```\nPOST /api/tokens      HTTP=401\nGET  /api/tokens/list HTTP=401\n/v1/usage             HTTP=401\nINFO Generated a bootstrap admin token; admin endpoints are closed\nINFO Admin UI disabled (set --admin-port / ADMIN_PORT to enable)\n```\n\nPlacing the copy before `COPY src/ src/` keeps the layer cache useful: UI assets change less often than Rust sources.\n\n## Why CI did not catch it\n\n`.github/workflows/release.yml` runs `docker/build-push-action` — but only in the release job, i.e. *after* a version has been tagged and cut. Nothing builds the image on a pull request, so a Dockerfile that cannot build merges cleanly and only fails once it is already released.\n\nWorth adding a `docker build` (no push) step to the PR checks. It is the one artifact users are told to deploy, and it is currently the only part of the build not exercised before release.\n","createdAt":"2026-08-08T15:11:18Z","number":59,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Docker build is broken on main: Dockerfile never copies the committed ui/dist that RustEmbed requires","updatedAt":"2026-08-08T16:01:08Z","url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/router/issues/59"}
